40320
720
\displaystyle\frac{{720}}{{40320}} (or reduced fraction \displaystyle\frac{{1}}{{56}}) or decimal 0.0179
Contestants A, B, C, D, E, F, G,  and I are in a 10K race.
(a) How many different ways can a race with 8 runners be completed? (Assume there is no tie.)

The order in which the runners complete the race matters so use Permutations


Number of different ways \displaystyle{8} runners can complete race =  \displaystyle{8}{P}{8}={40320} 
(b) In how many ways can G finish first and D finish second?


Ways G finishes first x Ways D finishes second x Ways that the remaining \displaystyle{6} contestants can complete the race


= 1 x 1 x \displaystyle{6}{P}{6}={720}
(c) Probability that G finishes first and D finishes second


\displaystyle=\frac{\text{Number of ways G finishes first and D finishes second}}{\text{Number of different ways 8 runners can complete race}}


\displaystyle=\frac{{720}}{{40320}}
